\title{Comparative Benchmark of State-of-Charge Observers and Physics-Informed Neural Networks Across Battery Aging and Thermal Regimes}

\keywords{State-of-charge, Lithium-ion battery, Battery degradation, Dual Extended Kalman filter, Physics-informed neural network, Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, Embedded BMS, ASME JEECS}

\begin{abstract}
Although battery State-of-Charge (SOC) estimation has been extensively investigated, existing comparative studies predominantly evaluate fresh cells at room temperature, obscuring algorithmic vulnerabilities under operational aging and thermal extremes. This work establishes a dual-tier benchmark of six representative nonlinear observers, deep recurrent networks, and physics-informed architectures (EKF, AEKF, DEKF, SMO, BiLSTM-Attn, and PINN-SOC) combining direct experimental cycler datasets with calibrated electro-thermal-aging co-simulation. Methodologies are systematically assessed across progressive capacity fade ($100\% \rightarrow 80\%$ SOH), wide ambient temperatures ($0^\circ\text{C}$ to $45^\circ\text{C}$), flat-plateau $\text{LiFePO}_4$ thermodynamics, and 8S series pack inconsistency. Results reveal that whereas uncompensated EKF suffers a 45.7-fold RMSE escalation ($0.065\%$ to $2.973\%$) as interfacial impedance expands, online parameter-tracking DEKF confines lifespan RMSE to $0.585\%$. Furthermore, we formulate a hybrid Physics-Informed Dual Kalman Filter (PIDKF) that reveals chemistry-dependent complementarity—neural overpotential compensation dominates on sloping-OCV NMC ($0.414\%$ RMSE), whereas dynamic hysteresis tracking dominates on flat-plateau LFP ($0.149\%$ RMSE) under calibrated co-simulation for the embedded exogenous-Jacobian configuration ($0.412\%$ and $0.148\%$ for exact Jacobian in Table~\ref{tab:9_pidkf}). Finally, bare-metal profiling on ARM Cortex-M microcontrollers ($14.20\;\upmu\mathrm{s}$ measured on Cortex-M4; $4.97\;\upmu\mathrm{s}$ constant-IPC clock-scaled estimate on Cortex-M7) delineates the Pareto efficiency frontier for industrial battery management systems.
\end{abstract}

