\subsection{Phase 5: Multi-Attribute Radar Trade-Off and Pareto Analysis}
Figure~\ref{fig:radar} synthesizes algorithmic trade-offs across 5 normalized dimensions: Nominal Accuracy, Aging Robustness, Thermal Robustness, Convergence Speed, and Computational Efficiency. 

The radar plot highlights that no single classical algorithm dominates across all attributes: EKF excels in simplicity and fresh-cell accuracy but collapses under aging, whereas DEKF offers superior degradation resilience, though its $0^\circ\text{C}$ transient sensitivity indicates that SMO or hybrid architectures are preferable in sub-zero climates where kinetics become strongly non-Arrhenius.

