%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Industrial BMS Implementation Guidelines}
From the Pareto frontier, four selection rules follow:
(1)~\emph{Premium EVs (NMC/LFP)}: \textbf{PIDKF} demonstrates superior degradation resilience ($0.414\%$ RMSE on aged NMC; $0.149\%$ on aged LFP at $85\%$ SOH); uncompensated EKF is discouraged due to 45.7-fold error surge.
(2)~\emph{Cost-Sensitive Storage (LFP)}: Deploy \textbf{DEKF} with dynamic hysteresis, bounding plateau RMSE to $0.870\%$ via open-loop Coulomb scaling without strain sensors.
(3)~\emph{Sensor Bias vs.\ EMI}: Deploy \textbf{EKF/DEKF} ($1.817\%\text{--}2.121\%$ RMSE) for minimum error under EMI, or \textbf{SMO} ($\mu = 0.02\text{ V}$) to bound drift ($1.024\%$).
(4)~\emph{Cloud-Edge Twins}: Execute real-time DEKF ($8.63\;\mu\text{s}$) or PIDKF ($14.20\;\mu\text{s}$; $0.227\%$ load for 16 cells @ $100\text{ ms}$) on MCUs, offloading deep PINNs to cloud diagnostics.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Conclusions}
Benchmarking six state estimation methodologies across ten operational phases yields five conclusions: 
(1)~\emph{Aging Degradation}: Uncompensated EKF suffers a 45.7-fold RMSE surge ($\text{ASF} = +4473.8\%$) as SOH fades to $80\%$, whereas parameter-tracking DEKF confines aged RMSE to $0.585\%$ ($\text{ASF} = +206.3\%$). 
(2)~\emph{EIS Correlation}: Randles--CPE Nyquist analysis links $>150\%$ $R_{\text{ct}}$ expansion to polarization mismatch. 
(3)~\emph{LFP Tracking}: Across flat $\text{LiFePO}_4$ plateaus, DEKF maintains $0.870\%$ RMSE by tracking Coulomb gain and ohmic drop without strain sensors. 
(4)~\emph{Pack Inconsistency}: Lumped observers incur $1.744\%$ RMSE on the weakest cell in an 8S pack, whereas distributed DEKF restricts weakest-cell error to $0.337\%$. 
(5)~\emph{Hybrid PIDKF}: Neural compensation dominates on aged NMC ($0.414\%$ RMSE) while hysteresis tracking dominates on aged LFP ($0.149\%$ RMSE), executing in $14.20\;\mu\text{s}$ ($2,386$ Cortex-M4 cycles).

