\appendix
\section{State-Space Matrices and Analytic Jacobians\label{app:jacobians}}
For 3-state NMC and 4-state LFP models, system matrices are $\mathbf{A}_k^{\text{NMC}} = \operatorname{diag}(1, a_1, a_2)$, $\mathbf{A}_k^{\text{LFP}} = \operatorname{diag}(1, a_1, a_2, a_{h,k})$, $\mathbf{H}_k^{\text{NMC}} = [V_{\text{ocv}}'(\hat{z}_k^-), -1, -1]$, and $\mathbf{H}_k^{\text{LFP}} = [\mathbf{H}_k^{\text{NMC}}, -1]$, with $a_i = e^{-\Delta t/\tau_i}$, $a_{h,k} = e^{-\beta|\Delta z_k|}$, $\mathbf{B}_k = [B_{1,k}, B_{2,k}, B_{3,k}, (0)]^T$, $\mathbf{g}_k = [0, 0, 0, (1 - a_{h,k}) M(z_k) \operatorname{sgn}(I_k)]^T$, and $\mathbf{C}_{\theta,k} = [-I_k, -\tfrac{\eta \Delta t I_{k-1}}{3600} V_{\text{ocv}}'(\hat{z}_k^+)]$. Locally ($a_{h,k} \approx a_h$), $|\det(\mathcal{O}_{n,k})| = V_{\text{ocv}}'(z_k) \prod_{i=1}^{n-1}(1 - a_i) \prod_{i < j} |a_i - a_j|$; full rank requires $V_{\text{ocv}}' > 0$, $I_k \ne 0$, and non-resonance $a_{h,k} \ne a_1, a_2$. On the plateau ($20\%\text{--}80\%$ SOC), constant saturation $M(z) \equiv M_0 = 30\text{ mV}$ renders $\mathbf{A}_k^{\text{LFP}}$ block-diagonal with spectrum $(1, a_1, a_2, a_{h,k})$, yielding determinant Eq.~\eqref{eqn:det_obs_lfp}. Evaluated numerically across $M = 1,370$ sliding windows ($N=30\text{ s}$) over UDDS cycles ($80\%\text{--}100\%$ SOH) under normalization $\tilde{\mathbf{x}} = [z, U_1/0.1, U_2/0.1, V_h/0.03]^T$ and PE ($\|I\|_{[k,k+N]} \ge 0.5\text{ A}$), minimum LTV Gramian singular value satisfies $\lambda_{\min}(\mathcal{G}_o) \ge 1.42 \times 10^{-3}$ at $25^\circ\text{C}$ ($\ge 1.18 \times 10^{-3}$ at $0^\circ\text{C}$; $\ge 1.55 \times 10^{-3}$ at $45^\circ\text{C}$), empirically confirming uniform complete observability across dynamic drive cycles to complement local analytical rank.

\section{Discrete Quasi-Sliding Mode Stability and UUB of SMO\label{app:lyapunov}}
Along sliding manifold $S_k = V_{\text{meas},k} - \hat{V}_{t,k}$, one-step dynamics follow $S_{k+1} = S_k + \Delta f_k - \gamma(\hat{z}_k) \operatorname{sat}(S_k/\mu)$ with scheduled gain $\gamma(\hat{z}) \equiv \mathbf{H}_k\mathbf{L}(\hat{z}) = l_{\text{smo}}$ ($V_{\text{ocv}}' \ge \alpha_{\min}$) and modeling disturbance $\Delta f_k = -R_0\Delta I_k + [V_{\text{ocv}}'(\xi_{k+1}) - V_{\text{ocv}}'(\xi_k)] e_{z,k} - V_{\text{ocv}}'\Delta Q_k + \sum_{i=1}^2 [(1-a_i)e_{U_i,k} - d_{U_i,k}] + [(1-a_{h,k})e_{h,k} - \Delta M_k] + (v_{k+1} - v_k)$, where $\Delta I_k = I_{k+1} - I_k$, capacity mismatch satisfies $V_{\text{ocv}}'\Delta Q_k = V_{\text{ocv}}'\frac{\eta\Delta t|I_k|}{3600}|\frac{1}{Q_{\text{act}}} - \frac{1}{\hat{Q}_{\text{act}}}| \le 0.35\text{ mV}$, and $v_k$ denotes bounded AFE noise ($|v_k| \le V_{\text{AFE}} \le 0.84\text{ mV}$, Arbin $\pm 0.02\%$ F.S.; distinct from filter $R_v$). Under nominal cycles ($\le 2.5\text{C}$ NMC, $\le 2\text{C}$ LFP; $|\Delta I_k| \le 0.025\text{ A}$): for NMC ($\bar{e}_h = 0$), $|\Delta f_k^{\text{NMC}}| \le 1.25\text{ mV} (R_0|\Delta I|) + 0.70\text{ mV} (\delta V_{\text{ocv}}') + 0.35\text{ mV} (\Delta Q) + 0.20\text{ mV} (\text{RC}) + 1.68\text{ mV} (2V_{\text{AFE}}) = 4.18\text{ mV} \le \Phi_d \equiv 0.005\text{ V}$; for LFP ($M_0 = 30\text{ mV}$, $\bar{e}_h = 60\text{ mV}$, $\Delta z \le 0.00056$), $(1-a_{h,k})\bar{e}_h \le (1-e^{-45\times 0.00056}) \times 60\text{ mV} = 1.49\text{ mV}$, yielding $|\Delta f_k^{\text{LFP}}| \le 1.25 + 0.10 + 0.10 + 0.20 + 1.49 + 1.68 = 4.82\text{ mV} \le \Phi_d \equiv 0.005\text{ V}$. At $4\text{C}$ pulses, $|\Delta f_k| \le \Phi_{d,4\text{C}} = 6.16\text{ mV} < 2\mu - l_{\text{smo}} = 15\text{ mV}$, preserving reaching decrement $\eta_{\text{reach},4\text{C}} = 8.84\text{ mV} > 0$ and ultimate set $r_{\text{ult},4\text{C}} = 8.21\text{ mV} < \mu$ (Phase~7 faults with $I_{\text{bias}} = 0.25\text{ A}$ and $\text{EMI} = 25\text{ mV}$ exceed $\Phi_d$, benchmarking graceful degradation). With candidate $V_k = \frac{1}{2} S_k^2$, increment $\Delta V_k = \frac{1}{2}(S_{k+1} - S_k)(S_{k+1} + S_k)$ satisfies: 
(1)~\emph{Contraction}: Outside $\mathcal{B}_\mu \equiv \{|S| \le \mu\}$, $\operatorname{sat}(S_k/\mu) = \operatorname{sgn}(S_k)$, yielding $S_{k+1} - S_k = -l_{\text{smo}}\operatorname{sgn}(S_k) + \Delta f_k$ and $S_{k+1} + S_k = 2S_k - l_{\text{smo}}\operatorname{sgn}(S_k) + \Delta f_k$. Condition $\Phi_d < l_{\text{smo}} < 2\mu - \Phi_d$ ($\Phi_d = 0.005\text{ V} < l_{\text{smo}} = 0.025\text{ V} < 0.035\text{ V}$) ensures $\Delta V_k < 0$, ensuring decrement $\eta_{\text{reach}} = \min(l_{\text{smo}} - \Phi_d, 2\mu - l_{\text{smo}} - \Phi_d) = 0.010\text{ V}$ ($|S_k| - |S_{k+1}| \ge \eta_{\text{reach}}$), entering $\mathcal{B}_\mu$ in $k^* \le \lceil (|S_0| - \mu)/\eta_{\text{reach}} \rceil$ steps. 
(2)~\emph{Invariance}: Inside $\mathcal{B}_\mu$, $S_{k+1} = (1 - l_{\text{smo}}/\mu)S_k + \Delta f_k$. Since $|1 - l_{\text{smo}}/\mu| = 0.25 < 1$, boundary $\Omega_{\text{ult}} \equiv \{|S| \le \frac{\Phi_d}{1 - |1 - l_{\text{smo}}/\mu|} = 6.67\text{ mV}\} \subset \mathcal{B}_\mu$ is positively invariant. 
(3)~\emph{UUB}: Perturbations satisfy $|d_{U_i,k}| \le (1 - a_i)\tilde{D}_{U_i}$ with $\tilde{D}_{U_i} \equiv R_i(T,\text{SOH}) I_{\text{bias}} + \delta R_i I_{\text{RMS}} \le 3.5\text{ mV}$ across $0^\circ\text{C}\text{--}45^\circ\text{C}$ ($\le 2.2\text{ mV}$ at $25^\circ\text{C}$), yielding tight ISS bounds $|e_{U_i}| \le \bar{e}_{U_i} \le 3.5\text{ mV}$ ($l_2=l_3=0$); LFP hysteresis satisfies $|e_h| \le 2 M_0 \equiv \bar{e}_h = 60\text{ mV}$ ($l_h=0$; $\bar{e}_h = 0$ for NMC). By MVT, $|e_{z,k}| \le (\mu + 2\bar{e}_{U} + \bar{e}_h + V_{\text{AFE}})/\alpha$. For NMC ($\alpha_{\text{NMC}} \ge 0.40\text{ V}$), state error is quantitatively tight ($|e_z| \le 7.2\%$ across $T$ and SOH; $\le 6.4\%$ at $25^\circ\text{C}$). For LFP ($\alpha_{\text{LFP}} = 0.00275\text{ V}$), finite UUB $\|\mathbf{e}_x\| < \infty$ is analytically guaranteed, while dynamic hysteresis co-estimation restricts empirical RMSE to $0.941\%$ (fresh) and $0.149\%$ (PIDKF aged). 

