Under the Joseph-stabilized Riccati difference equation:
\begin{align}
\mathbf{P}_{k+1}^- &= \mathbf{A}_k \mathbf{P}_k^+ \mathbf{A}_k^T + \mathbf{Q}_k, \label{eqn:riccati_pred}\\
\mathbf{P}_k^+ &= (\mathbf{I} - \mathbf{K}_k \mathbf{H}_k)\mathbf{P}_k^-(\mathbf{I} - \mathbf{K}_k \mathbf{H}_k)^T + \mathbf{K}_k R_{\text{eff},k} \mathbf{K}_k^T, \label{eqn:riccati_upd}
\end{align}
the discrete algebraic Riccati operator maps the positive definite cone $\mathbb{S}_{++}^n$ into itself. Because $\mathbf{A}_k$ is contractive ($|\lambda_i(\mathbf{A}_k)| \le 1$), process covariance satisfies $\underline{q}\mathbf{I} \preceq \mathbf{Q}_k \preceq \bar{q}\mathbf{I}$, and innovation covariance satisfies $0 < \underline{r} \le R_{\text{eff},k} \le \bar{r} < \infty$, the uniform complete observability (UCO) condition $\mathcal{G}_o(k, k+N) \succeq \alpha_o \mathbf{I}$ establishes that the Riccati mapping is strictly contractive under the Riemannian metric on $\mathbb{S}_{++}^n$. By the discrete Kalman-Bucy theorem, the prior and posterior error covariances are uniformly upper- and lower-bounded for all $k \ge N$:
\begin{equation}\label{eqn:riccati_bounds}
\underline{p} \mathbf{I} \preceq \mathbf{P}_k^+ \preceq \mathbf{P}_k^- \preceq \bar{p} \mathbf{I},
\end{equation}
with explicit bounds $\underline{p} = \underline{q} > 0$ and $\bar{p} = (\alpha_o^{-1} + N \bar{q})\bar{a}^{2N} < \infty$. Consequently, the Kalman gain $\|\mathbf{K}_k\|_2 \le \bar{p} \|\mathbf{H}_k\|_2 / \underline{r} \le \bar{K} < \infty$ remains uniformly bounded across all operational drive cycles, preventing covariance divergence and validating the UUB stochastic stability theorems in Section~3.7 and Appendix~B. 


